# DebDroid rootfs manifest
#
# The debian filesystems DebDroid can install, and where to get them.
#
# Checksums live here, in the repository, deliberately: they travel with the
# scripts and are reviewable in the commit history, so a payload's checksum
# never comes from the same place as the payload. See docs/reference/integrity.md.
#
# A TARBALL entry is preferred over an IMAGE entry. A tarball carries no
# filesystem, so the image is always created locally by busybox's ext2-only
# mkfs.ext2 and a modern mke2fs can never put features in it that old phone
# kernels refuse to mount. An IMAGE entry must additionally record its
# filesystem and feature flags.
#
# Format, one record per line, fields separated by "|":
#   id | kind | arch | release | sha256 | size | url [ | mirror-url ... ]
#
#   kind     TARBALL or IMAGE
#   arch     the debian architecture, matching check_arch
#   size     uncompressed bytes, used to pick a sensible default image size
#
# Checksums below are placeholders until the tarballs are built and published;
# the bootstrap refuses any entry whose checksum does not verify, so an
# unfilled entry fails closed rather than installing something unverified.

# bookworm-arm64 | TARBALL | arm64 | bookworm | PLACEHOLDER | 0 | https://github.com/NICUP14/DebDroid/releases/download/rootfs-bookworm/debian-bookworm-arm64.tar.gz
# bookworm-armhf | TARBALL | armhf | bookworm | PLACEHOLDER | 0 | https://github.com/NICUP14/DebDroid/releases/download/rootfs-bookworm/debian-bookworm-armhf.tar.gz
